course: dictionary
lesson: 8879
title: Words for people: shouter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shouter is a noun, a word for a person. It comes from the verb shout, and the ending -er tells you it is a person who does the action. A shouter shouts a lot, or speaks very loudly.
explain: Read the context: «Children copy the adults around them, so a coach who shouts insults can turn players into shouters too.» The coach shouts insults, and the players learn to do the same. Here a shouter is someone who yells, and the clue is the word insults.
explain: Shouters can be parents, teachers or sports coaches. On the sideline, a shouter may cheer loudly or complain loudly. Notice the feeling behind the word: a shouter often gets angry quickly.
fact: A shouter is a person who shouts a lot or speaks very loudly.
fact: «Shouter» is a noun, and its plural is «shouters».
fact: A shouter often gets angry quickly and yells when cross.
fact: In sport, a shouter on the sideline cheers or complains loudly.
fact: If shouting at home feels scary, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Children copy the adults around them, so a coach who shouts insults can turn players into shouters too.» What is a shouter? | *A person who shouts a lot or speaks very loudly | A person who keeps very quiet and whispers | A kind of sports ball | A small brown bird
exercise: What might a shouter on the sideline do? | *Cheer or complain loudly | Whisper secret plans | Fall asleep under the bench | Sit silently reading a book
exercise: Which feeling often goes with being a shouter? | Wanting to fly | *Getting angry quickly and yelling when cross | Being bored of music | Feeling sleepy after lunch
test: Why might a child tell a trusted adult about a shouter at home? | *Because shouting at home feels scary | Because the adult has a new car | Because the adult is a good cook | Because the shouting at home feels scary
test: The ending -er in shouter tells you it is a what? | A place | A colour | A question | *A person who does the action
exam: In «so a coach who shouts insults can turn players into shouters too», what does shouters mean? | Players who score goals | *People who shout a lot and yell when cross | Teachers who give homework | Quiet people who whisper
